[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m To find the sum of all integer bases \( b > 9 \) for which \( 17_b \) divides \( 97_b \), we start by expressing these numbers in base 10. 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m The number \( 17_b \) in base 10 is \( 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m The number \( 97_b \) in base 10 is \( 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m We need to find \( b \) such that \( b + 7 \) divides \( 9b + 7 \). This translates to solving the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 9b + 7 = k(b + 7)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m where \( k \) is an integer. Expanding and simplifying this equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 9b + 7 = kb + 7k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 9b - kb = 7k - 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m For \( b \) to be an integer, \( 9 - k \) must be a divisor of \( 7(k - 1) \). Testing possible values of \( k \) (divisors of 7: 1, 7, -1, -7), we find that only \( k = 8 \) gives a valid integer solution.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m Thus, substituting \( k = 8 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m b = \frac{7(8 - 1)}{9 - 8} = \frac{49}{1} = 49
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=268047)[0m Therefore, the only valid base \( b \) is 49. The sum of all such bases is:
